{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1531500-what-is-the-population-of-mortal-with-supernatural-merit","id":1531500,"title":"What is the population of Mortal with Supernatural Merit?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-26T02:03:38-08:00","id":1531500,"title":"What is the population of Mortal with Supernatural Merit?","content":"It's seem that theotheoretically any Mortal have the potential to have Supernatural Merit? But what is the actual percentage of people who actually have it? I'm thinking about 5-8% of the World Population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T07:13:43-08:00","id":1531511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1531500-what-is-the-population-of-mortal-with-supernatural-merit#post1531500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's seem that theotheoretically any Mortal have the potential to have Supernatural Merit? But what is the actual percentage of people who actually have it? I'm thinking about 5-8% of the World Population.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say considerably less than that, since even 1% of the world population would mean <b><i>more than 80 million people</i></b> with Supernatural merit. That is almost the whole population of Germany, the most populous country of Europe outside of Russia. <b>Really </b>a lot of people indeed.<br /> <br /> <br /> For the sake of reference, i would like to point out that vampiric population statistics amidst when given tended to gravitate somewhere between 1:100K to 1:20K in some pretty crowded/stacked places. Supposing that Uratha, Awakened, Lost &amp; Geisters have similar proportions - what may or not be true due to a number of factors, we would get 5 supernatural beings amidst 20 thousand people, or 25 major supernaturals in a 100 thousand people town/city.<br /> <br /> That same hypotethical town would have <b><i>one thousand people</i></b> with the Supernatural merit, so 40 people with weird tricks of their own per individual with a major template. <b>Quite</b> the lynch mob+ out and about, only accounting for 1% of the World Population, that is much less than what you proposed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T07:44:49-08:00","id":1531513,"title":"","content":"There's no answer to this even hinted at in the books, as far as I'm aware. I'm sure if you asked the authors you'd get something along the lines of &quot;however many the story requires.&quot; <br /> <br /> Generally, though, I'd go much lower than that. Even 1% of the world would be some 80 million people. In comparison the number of Uratha (or perhaps just Forsaken, I'm uncertain) in 1st edition was roughly 500,000 and the number of vampires was roughly 80,000. I doubt the number of all the splats together equalled a million total. (Obviously ghosts and spirits and the like are exceptions, I'm only talking about the splats themselves.) <br /> <br /> So if you go with say roughly 1 million people having supernatural merits, that's probably roughly equal to the rough number of members of splats around the world based on 1st edition numbers (unless the werewolf numbers were Forsaken specifically). Even if you want double or triple that number, you're still looking at significantly less than 1%.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T07:50:12-08:00","id":1531514,"title":"","content":"Maybe I was being a little optomistic with the Number of People that have Supernatural Merit, but I think it's definetly more than 1% of World of Population, maybe 2.5%, since Supernatural Merit is Diverse, and Hunter can have Supernatural Merit, which would increase the chance of them having something to level the playing field. And not all Supernatural Merit is obvious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28270,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","user":"Yumlum","date":". 02-26-2024, 10:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T09:02:37-08:00","id":1531525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1531500-what-is-the-population-of-mortal-with-supernatural-merit#post1531500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's seem that theotheoretically any Mortal have the potential to have Supernatural Merit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind that because a Merit is mechanically available to characters of a given type does not mean any character of a given type can pick it up like ordering items off a menu. A player can, with Storyteller's consent, but every human in the Chronicles of Darkness is not being puppeted by a player who is making character build decisions for them.<br /> <br /> Most Supernatural Merits are rare, unexplained anomalies, not skills or talents that can be honed or picked up. A vampire can learn Celerity. A human generally cannot &quot;learn&quot; Telekinesis. Either they have it or they don't, and they usually don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T14:21:58-08:00","id":1531546,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think that most people treat/think of Supernatural Merits as much more common than they actually are, especially as for a Mortal game they are very advantageous and with the prerequisites being &quot;Mortal&quot;, unless the ST would forbid them then they are a very common pick. However, the text seems to suggest that they are relatively rare, such as being accessible to Stigmatics is considered to be a special advantage, and certain people having one or two of those is considered to make them very &quot;special&quot;. Basically, they suffer from the &quot;protagonist syndrome&quot;, where because those abilities are often used by the main characters, it is easy to believe that most characters have them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T15:26:43-08:00","id":1531551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1531500-what-is-the-population-of-mortal-with-supernatural-merit?p=1531513#post1531513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no answer to this even hinted at in the books, as far as I'm aware. I'm sure if you asked the authors you'd get something along the lines of &quot;however many the story requires.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This bares additional emphasis.<br /> <br /> There isn't supposed to be an expected number. Even Vampire moved away from that hold over from the WoD more and more as time went on.<br /> <br /> The CofD, broadly as a setting, is supposed to be mysterious. That means there can't be a certain level detail or you lose the tone of the setting. The setting needs to be able to accommodate a small town were virtually everyone has some supernatural ability, as well as a large city that is apparently completely devoid of any kind of supernatural activity of any kind. Allowing for wild amounts of local variations means every new location is different; and thus mysterious.<br /> <br /> That's why, &quot;what the story requires,&quot; is the most important metric instead of some global population demographics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T20:47:15-08:00","id":1531580,"title":"","content":"With all of that in mind, I still think that at least 1% of the World Population have Supernatural Merit, since during Dark Era Lifiting the Veil, more people start to gain Psychic Power that they have no explination for. And I'm not just talking about specific type of Supernatural Merit, Mortal with any type of Supernatural Merit, which I think is more than a few thousand people. And with the existence of Supernatural Merit Template mean that there is multiple society of Mortal with Supernatural Merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T22:01:00-08:00","id":1531586,"title":"","content":"I think maybe you're underestimating just how many people 1% of the world population is.<br /> <br /> (Also, the population of people with Supernatural Merits isn't equal to the number of people with some kind of touch of the supernatural. There's probably some people with some subtle flicker in them that is spooky but not advantageous, reliable, or mechanically meaningful enough to describe in terms of traits that cost chargen/advancement resources.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-27T00:00:31-08:00","id":1531601,"title":"","content":"Would number of Mortal with Supernatural Merit outnumbered every other splat combine?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-27T00:26:34-08:00","id":1531603,"title":"","content":"Why does it matter?<br /> <br /> Seriously. The game doesn't care. The game isn't trying to simulate the CofD as full reality where these things can be studied and theoretically have your questions answered. No character is ever going to know. You don't need a global number to make whatever game you're running work; it's easier to make your personal games work when you're not beholden to some arbitrary number from the books.<br /> <br /> You've asked a question, and you've gotten the answer. It doesn't seem like an answer you like. But it's the answer. Are you looking for more?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-27T02:58:47-08:00","id":1531608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1531500-what-is-the-population-of-mortal-with-supernatural-merit?p=1531580#post1531580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...since during Dark Era Lifiting the Veil, more people start to gain Psychic Power that they have no explination for.</div> </div> </div> </div>The default setting is the modern-day, not 1885-90. Like, it doesn't explain exactly the uptick in psychics/mediums, but it's very clearly tied to the Avernian Gates opening; something that isn't true in the modern-day.<br /> <br /> Also, even during those years, <i>Lifting the Veil</i> gives rough numbers that are still very small. Like, the conceit of the chapter is that the Spiritualist movement is basically the same as in the real-world, it's just that some of the claimants can really do what they claim. The 'default' it gives is that about 1 in 10 mediums are actually real. In this period, that's 1 in 3. That's a big increase, but it's a big increase inside a very shallow pool.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-27T03:01:33-08:00","id":1531609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1531500-what-is-the-population-of-mortal-with-supernatural-merit?p=1531580#post1531580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With all of that in mind, I still think that at least 1% of the World Population have Supernatural Merit, since during Dark Era Lifiting the Veil, more people start to gain Psychic Power that they have no explination for. And I'm not just talking about specific type of Supernatural Merit, Mortal with any type of Supernatural Merit, which I think is more than a few thousand people. And with the existence of Supernatural Merit Template mean that there is multiple society of Mortal with Supernatural Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>1% of the world population is much higher than &quot;a few thousand people.&quot; But do whatever you want so long as it makes a good story. I can totally imagine a society where having merits can put someone into a different 1% than we have now and how they in turn could shape society. <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}